<% layout('layouts/boilerplate') %>

<div class="container py-5">
  <div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-lg-10">
      
      <!-- Page Header -->
      <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm rounded-4 p-4 p-md-5 mb-4 bg-white">
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <div class="ta-icon-wrapper icon-purple fs-3 mb-0">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-file-contract"></i>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="badge bg-purple-subtle text-purple rounded-pill px-3 py-1 fw-semibold small">Terms of Service</span>
            <h1 class="fw-bold display-6 mb-0 mt-1">Terms & Conditions</h1>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted mb-0 fs-6">
          Please read these terms before exploring or contributing travel content on TravelAtlas.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Content Card -->
      <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm rounded-4 p-4 p-md-5 bg-white">
        <div class="space-y-4">

          <section class="mb-4">
            <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-handshake text-primary me-2"></i>1. Acceptance of Terms</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed">
              By accessing or using TravelAtlas, creating a registered traveler profile, or contributing travel guides and reviews, you agree to comply with and be bound by these Terms & Conditions and our Community Guidelines.
            </p>
          </section>

          <hr class="my-4 text-light-subtle" />

          <section class="mb-4">
            <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-compass text-info me-2"></i>2. Platform Purpose</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed">
              TravelAtlas is an open, community-driven travel knowledge repository designed to centralize sightseeing information, parking tips, best visit seasons, and crowd metrics into single canonical pages. TravelAtlas is an informational platform and does not offer booking, ticketing, or reservation services.
            </p>
          </section>

          <hr class="my-4 text-light-subtle" />

          <section class="mb-4">
            <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-copy text-warning me-2"></i>3. Single Canonical Page Policy</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed">
              To prevent fragmented information, TravelAtlas enforces a single canonical page per sightseeing destination. Users agree to utilize existing destination pages to submit reviews, photos, and tips rather than creating duplicate entries for the same location.
            </p>
          </section>

          <hr class="my-4 text-light-subtle" />

          <section class="mb-4">
            <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-pen-nib text-success me-2"></i>4. User Content & Intellectual Property</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed">
              You retain ownership of the photos, reviews, and travel tips you submit. By posting content on TravelAtlas, you grant the platform a non-exclusive, royalty-free license to display, format, and share your contributions on the destination pages and public discovery feeds.
            </p>
          </section>

          <hr class="my-4 text-light-subtle" />

          <section class="mb-4">
            <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-ban text-danger me-2"></i>5. Prohibited Activities</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-2">Users agree not to:</p>
            <ul class="text-secondary leading-relaxed">
              <li>Submit false, deceptive, or intentionally misleading travel metrics or location details.</li>
              <li>Post offensive, abusive, defamatory, or inappropriate content or images.</li>
              <li>Attempt to bypass security features, rate limiters, or authentication mechanisms.</li>
              <li>Use TravelAtlas for unsolicited commercial advertising or spam.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <hr class="my-4 text-light-subtle" />

          <section>
            <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation text-secondary me-2"></i>6. Limitation of Information</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-0">
              Travel content is crowdsourced from community travelers. While we encourage accuracy, weather conditions, forest permissions, ticket fees, and road accessibility can change. Travelers are advised to cross-verify critical transit information locally.
            </p>
          </section>

        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>
